WEBVTT

00:03.880 --> 00:05.480
Okay, so what is between?

00:05.520 --> 00:09.680
It's going to go and check if a value falls within a specific range.

00:09.680 --> 00:14.400
So you have a range and you are checking whether your value is in the range or outside the range.

00:14.400 --> 00:16.600
So let's understand exactly what this means okay.

00:16.640 --> 00:19.920
So now in order to build a range you need two things.

00:19.920 --> 00:22.560
You need the lower boundary for the range.

00:22.560 --> 00:24.920
And you need as well the upper boundary.

00:24.920 --> 00:27.840
Once you have two boundaries then you have a range.

00:27.840 --> 00:33.960
And everything between those two boundaries is going to be true, and everything outside those boundaries

00:33.960 --> 00:35.000
is going to be false.

00:35.000 --> 00:40.160
So now, for example, let's say that we have the lower boundary 100 and the upper boundary 500.

00:40.200 --> 00:44.720
And there is one thing that you have to understand about the between the boundaries are inclusive.

00:44.720 --> 00:51.360
So that means if a value is exactly 100 or exactly 500, then it's going to be considered as a true.

00:51.360 --> 00:54.000
So it is considered to be inside the range.

00:54.000 --> 01:00.720
Now, if you apply this filter to our data, where we say the score must be between 100 and 500 scale,

01:00.760 --> 01:02.000
going to go and do the following.

01:02.040 --> 01:07.680
So for the first customer, Mariam is going to go and check whether her score is inside the boundaries.

01:07.730 --> 01:10.890
So as you can see, 300 is between 100 and 500.

01:10.890 --> 01:12.650
So she is in the green area.

01:12.650 --> 01:16.450
And that's why it's going to be happy about it and leave the customer in the outputs.

01:16.490 --> 01:17.490
Now moving on to John.

01:17.490 --> 01:18.850
John has 900.

01:18.890 --> 01:21.610
As you can see 900 is greater than 500.

01:21.610 --> 01:25.330
So this value is going to be outside the boundaries on the right side.

01:25.330 --> 01:28.210
And this means the score of John is not in the range.

01:28.210 --> 01:33.930
That's why he is not fulfilling the condition and is going to go and remove this customer from the results.

01:33.970 --> 01:36.130
Now moving on to George 750.

01:36.170 --> 01:41.730
The same thing outside the range scale will not accept it and remove the customer from the final results.

01:41.770 --> 01:43.050
Now moving on to Martin.

01:43.050 --> 01:47.090
His score is 500 and this is exactly at the boundary.

01:47.090 --> 01:49.810
So if it's like 501 it's going to be outside.

01:49.810 --> 01:53.770
So since between is inclusive then SQL is going to accept it.

01:53.770 --> 01:57.370
And Martin considered to be in the range and fulfilling the condition.

01:57.370 --> 01:59.370
So it's going to keep him in the final results.

01:59.410 --> 02:01.010
Now we are speaking about bitter.

02:01.170 --> 02:04.290
He has zero score and this is less than 100.

02:04.290 --> 02:06.410
So in the left side not in the range.

02:06.410 --> 02:09.410
So not fulfilling the condition and SQL going to go and remove him.

02:09.410 --> 02:11.970
This is exactly how between works in SQL.

02:11.970 --> 02:12.770
It's very simple.

02:12.810 --> 02:13.010
Okay.

02:13.050 --> 02:14.330
So now we have the following task.

02:14.410 --> 02:20.730
and it says retrieve all customers whose score falls in range between 100 and 500.

02:20.770 --> 02:26.330
So let's start as usual by selecting all data from customers and execute it.

02:26.370 --> 02:27.970
Now the task says everything.

02:27.970 --> 02:32.810
We need all customers in a range, so we have a lower value and a higher value.

02:32.810 --> 02:35.610
So in order to do that, as usual we can use the where.

02:35.610 --> 02:38.530
And then we're going to specify the column that we want to filter on.

02:38.530 --> 02:39.690
So it's going to be the score.

02:39.690 --> 02:44.570
And since we have like two boundaries we can go and use the function between and we start with the first

02:44.570 --> 02:46.250
boundary, the lowest boundary.

02:46.250 --> 02:52.210
So it is the 105 hundred the high boundary, the upper boundary.

02:52.210 --> 02:54.970
So between 100 and 500.

02:54.970 --> 02:56.730
So now let's go and execute it.

02:56.730 --> 03:01.890
And with that we get only those two customers because they are between this window.

03:01.890 --> 03:04.210
Now there is another way in how to solve this task.

03:04.210 --> 03:09.890
By not using between, we can go and use the comparison operator together with a logical operator.

03:09.890 --> 03:12.090
And so let me show you how we can do that.

03:12.090 --> 03:13.730
I'm going to go and copy the whole thing.

03:13.770 --> 03:15.650
And now we're going to write two conditions.

03:15.650 --> 03:22.700
So first the score should be higher or equal to 100 because the boundaries is inclusive and the other

03:22.700 --> 03:26.540
one the score is less or equal to 500.

03:26.540 --> 03:28.140
So this is the upper boundary.

03:28.140 --> 03:29.780
So with that we have the two conditions.

03:29.780 --> 03:33.100
And we can go and connect them using the and operator.

03:33.100 --> 03:38.020
So it's like very similar to the between we have an and between the upper and the lower boundaries.

03:38.020 --> 03:40.580
But we are using the comparison operators.

03:40.580 --> 03:45.060
So it is higher or equal to 100 and lower or equal to 500.

03:45.100 --> 03:48.620
If you go and run this query you will get exactly same results.

03:48.660 --> 03:53.380
